1
00:00:00,340 --> 00:00:03,287
Bring the previous lessons together in one
workflow.

2
00:00:03,467 --> 00:00:07,329
Start with the issue and plan the smallest
verifiable change.

3
00:00:07,509 --> 00:00:12,457
Then demonstrate a failing regression,
apply the fix, and verify the passing

4
00:00:12,457 --> 00:00:13,173
regression.

5
00:00:13,353 --> 00:00:16,799
The author reviews the diff and submits
the pull request.

6
00:00:16,979 --> 00:00:19,437
A teammate reviews it independently.

7
00:00:19,617 --> 00:00:24,433
At each checkpoint, write down what
evidence lets the work continue and who

8
00:00:24,433 --> 00:00:25,717
makes that decision.

9
00:00:27,173 --> 00:00:32,495
Use the reusable prompt in Plan with the
issue, the validator file, and its tests.

10
00:00:32,675 --> 00:00:36,151
The agent proposes an edit and
verification steps.

11
00:00:36,331 --> 00:00:39,286
Review the suggestion against the issue
yourself.

12
00:00:39,466 --> 00:00:44,277
In this example, it may add a regression
test and change one comparison.

13
00:00:44,457 --> 00:00:50,220
If it proposes a new dependency or changes
the public interface, revise the plan with

14
00:00:50,220 --> 00:00:54,153
the original requirement visible before
moving into Agent.

15
00:00:55,632 --> 00:00:59,249
Add the new test first and run it using
the approved runner.

16
00:00:59,429 --> 00:01:04,975
A useful failure identifies the zero case
and shows that the validator returned

17
00:01:04,975 --> 00:01:05,326
true.

18
00:01:05,506 --> 00:01:10,462
If the failure comes from a broken import,
fix the test setup and repeat the run

19
00:01:10,462 --> 00:01:12,321
before accepting the evidence.

20
00:01:12,501 --> 00:01:16,394
The checkpoint requires a failing
assertion tied to the issue.

21
00:01:16,574 --> 00:01:20,786
Record the result and use it to justify
applying the small fix.

22
00:01:22,257 --> 00:01:24,564
Ask Agent to make the agreed edit.

23
00:01:24,744 --> 00:01:27,095
Check the diff and rerun the same suite.

24
00:01:27,275 --> 00:01:32,468
If another test starts failing or the
expected regression still fails, return to

25
00:01:32,468 --> 00:01:34,869
the fix and inspect the new behavior.

26
00:01:35,049 --> 00:01:38,314
In a passing run, capture the command and
the result.

27
00:01:38,494 --> 00:01:43,346
This pause keeps a plausible explanation
from becoming your only evidence.

28
00:01:43,526 --> 00:01:47,328
It also helps keep the next review focused
on the actual change.

29
00:01:48,798 --> 00:01:52,446
Use the skill from the previous lesson to
draft the handoff.

30
00:01:52,626 --> 00:01:56,819
Provide the linked training issue, the
diff, and the output you just checked.

31
00:01:56,999 --> 00:02:01,488
Review its draft and correct any claim
that does not match those artifacts.

32
00:02:01,668 --> 00:02:06,224
Push the feature branch and open the pull
request through your approved workflow.

33
00:02:06,404 --> 00:02:09,296
The configured checks run on the reviewed
change.

34
00:02:09,476 --> 00:02:14,158
A passing local or runner result gives the
reviewer additional evidence.

35
00:02:15,632 --> 00:02:19,343
The peer now uses the approved terminal
and their own account.

36
00:02:19,523 --> 00:02:23,799
They view the pull request, read the diff
and check the required results.

37
00:02:23,979 --> 00:02:27,532
If the evidence is sufficient, they can
submit an approval.

38
00:02:27,712 --> 00:02:32,662
If something is missing, they can request
changes and name what needs to be checked.

39
00:02:32,842 --> 00:02:37,310
The repository's configured checks and
review rules protect the merge.

40
00:02:37,490 --> 00:02:40,189
The agent's draft helps prepare the
handoff.

41
00:02:41,632 --> 00:02:45,622
Try the workflow with a teammate on the
synthetic repository.

42
00:02:45,802 --> 00:02:50,820
During the first run, walk all the way to
the peer decision with passing checks and

43
00:02:50,820 --> 00:02:51,666
a small patch.

44
00:02:51,846 --> 00:02:57,301
During the second, introduce missing test
evidence or a failing required check and

45
00:02:57,301 --> 00:02:58,564
say where you stop.

46
00:02:58,744 --> 00:03:02,328
Write down the evidence needed to resume
and who decides.

47
00:03:02,508 --> 00:03:05,923
That is the workflow you can reuse on the
next issue.
